<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Raylib on STEP Batch 12</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/</link><description>Recent content in Raylib on STEP Batch 12</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en_US</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:14:18 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Movement and Frame Time</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/frame_time/</link><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/frame_time/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="is-the-dinosaur-always-this-fast"&gt;Is the dinosaur always this fast?&lt;a class="anchor" href="#is-the-dinosaur-always-this-fast"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In the fourth part of &lt;a href="https://step-12.github.io/assignments/dino_run/#4-what-goes-up"&gt;The Long Run&lt;/a&gt;, we gave the dinosaur a velocity and gravity.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Your code may look different, but somewhere it probably does something like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;dino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;velocityY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;gravity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;dino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;velocityY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The velocity changes on every update. The position changes on every update too.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This produces a jump, but there is a problem hiding in it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="try-this-before-reading-further"&gt;Try this before reading further&lt;a class="anchor" href="#try-this-before-reading-further"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Find this line in your game:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Keyboard Events</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/keyboard_events/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/keyboard_events/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="can-we-play-yet"&gt;Can we play yet?&lt;a class="anchor" href="#can-we-play-yet"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We can draw a rectangle. We can change its colour. We can even make it move across the screen.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Now imagine watching that rectangle move from left to right. Again. And again.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It might be interesting for a little while.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But there is nothing for us to do. Whatever we press, the rectangle continues with its very important rectangle business.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That gets boring.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Think about a game you enjoy. What would happen if you could no longer control anything? The player runs by itself, jumps by itself, and wins or loses without your help.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Drawing Text</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/drawing_text/</link><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/drawing_text/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="drawing-text"&gt;Drawing text&lt;a class="anchor" href="#drawing-text"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;ve spent a lot of time drawing things such as rectangles, circles and lines.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But what if we want to put some words on the screen?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Raylib provides &lt;code&gt;DrawText&lt;/code&gt; for this.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The basic API looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;DrawText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Hello, Raylib!&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WHITE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The arguments are:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The text to draw.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The x-coordinate.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The y-coordinate.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The font size.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;The color.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;DrawText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Hello&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WHITE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;DrawText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Raylib&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;80&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;YELLOW&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The two pieces of text can have different positions, sizes and colors.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Textures</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/curves_textures/</link><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:44:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/curves_textures/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="additional-raylib-api"&gt;Additional Raylib API&lt;a class="anchor" href="#additional-raylib-api"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So far, we&amp;rsquo;ve learned how to draw a few basic shapes with Raylib.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;ve also learned how to work with &lt;a href="https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/raylib_objects/"&gt;objects in Raylib&lt;/a&gt;, including &lt;code&gt;Color&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Vector2&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In this post, we&amp;rsquo;ll add a few more tools to our drawing vocabulary:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;drawing onto a render texture&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The goal here is simple: &lt;strong&gt;learn what these APIs let us do and get comfortable using them.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We will not try to understand everything happening inside Raylib. Where there is an interesting idea underneath an API, we&amp;rsquo;ll take a brief look at it.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Worldly Woes</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/worldlywoes/</link><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:15:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/worldlywoes/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="the-woes-of-the-world"&gt;The Woes Of The World&lt;a class="anchor" href="#the-woes-of-the-world"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When we started writing Raylib programs, I gave you a template that used a &lt;code&gt;world&lt;/code&gt; object.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The idea was simple. We needed a way to share information between &lt;code&gt;setup()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;update()&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;draw()&lt;/code&gt;. So &lt;code&gt;setup()&lt;/code&gt; would create a world, and the other functions would use it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This was a reasonable idea.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, the world has grown in power. It now knows everything, goes everywhere, and is invited to functions that have absolutely no business meeting it.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Objects in Raylib</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/raylib_objects/</link><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/raylib_objects/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="objects-in-raylib"&gt;Objects in Raylib&lt;a class="anchor" href="#objects-in-raylib"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We have learned about objects in JavaScript.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So far, we have mostly looked at objects as a way of putting related information together:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;student&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Ravi&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;age&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The useful thing about this is not the curly braces. The useful thing is that we can give a shape to something we are thinking about.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Raylib has many things that naturally have more than one piece of information.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A colour has several components.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Template</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/template/</link><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:45:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/template/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="modules-and-a-raylib-template"&gt;Modules and a Raylib Template&lt;a class="anchor" href="#modules-and-a-raylib-template"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So far, each Raylib program you have written has lived in a single file.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We have already started organizing that file into functions:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WindowShouldClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This gives different parts of the program different responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But there is another kind of organization available to us.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We can separate our program into &lt;strong&gt;different files&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Skeleton</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/skeleton/</link><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:45:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/skeleton/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="organizing-a-raylib-program"&gt;Organizing a Raylib Program&lt;a class="anchor" href="#organizing-a-raylib-program"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You have now written a few small Raylib programs.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You have probably noticed that even a small program starts to contain several different kinds of code:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that prepares the window&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that changes things&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that draws things&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that keeps the program running&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It is useful to give these different responsibilities a little structure.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We are going to use the following skeleton:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is not a rule imposed by Raylib.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Simple exercises</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/first_exercises/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/first_exercises/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="first-exercises"&gt;First Exercises&lt;a class="anchor" href="#first-exercises"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You now have a working Raylib program.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You have seen how a Raylib program is structured, and you have used functions such as &lt;code&gt;r.DrawRectangle&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Now it is time to start solving some small problems.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;For these exercises, create a directory called:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;workspace/raylib_exercises/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Each exercise should be its own program.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Use these filenames:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;01_center_rectangle.js&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;02_center_rectangle_in_rectangle.js&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;03_scale_and_center.js&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;04_closer_target.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Write the Raylib program yourself for each exercise. You should not need to copy the program from the previous post.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raylib anatomy</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/anatomy/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/anatomy/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="the-anatomy-of-a-raylib-program"&gt;The anatomy of a Raylib program&lt;a class="anchor" href="#the-anatomy-of-a-raylib-program"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In the previous post, we saw that Raylib is a library that gives our JavaScript programs a collection of functions for working with graphics.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We are now going to look at a complete Raylib program.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Don&amp;rsquo;t worry if you don&amp;rsquo;t understand everything in it yet.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In fact, you shouldn&amp;rsquo;t.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Read through it once and see if you can recognize anything.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;require&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;raylib&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;InitWindow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Raylib&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SetTargetFPS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WindowShouldClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BeginDrawing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ClearBackground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;BLACK&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;DrawRectangle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WHITE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;EndDrawing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;CloseWindow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;There are quite a few things happening here.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Intro to Graphics/Raylib</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/intro/</link><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/intro/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="raylib"&gt;Raylib&lt;a class="anchor" href="#raylib"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So far, most of the programs you have written have produced things like numbers and text.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You might have written:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;and seen:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Or perhaps you wrote a function that takes some values, performs a computation, and returns another value.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;What if the result of our program could be something that we could &lt;strong&gt;see&lt;/strong&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;What if instead of producing:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;our program could produce a rectangle on the screen?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;That is where we are going next.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>